00:32:53.194 --> 00:32:57.286
So they called Joe [Conohan?] who was a white man.

732
00:32:57.286 --> 00:32:58.105
My boss.

733
00:32:58.105 --> 00:32:59.742
He says, "Wes here?

734
00:32:59.742 --> 00:33:04.652
Tell Wes he got a package he left in the front office."

735
00:33:04.652 --> 00:33:05.880
I was . . . Mail.

736
00:33:05.880 --> 00:33:07.517
I was delivering mail.

737
00:33:07.517 --> 00:33:10.790
"He need to come pick up this thing.

738
00:33:10.790 --> 00:33:14.473
And is he going to pick it up tomorrow?"

739
00:33:14.473 --> 00:33:18.565
They said, "No, no. Mr. Ratliff want it done today."

740
00:33:18.565 --> 00:33:24.703
Well he . . . Joe Conahan, my boss, he said, "Oh no, he got to come today.

741
00:33:24.703 --> 00:33:32.478
Tell him just come get it and pick it up and you can have it at your office tomorrow."

742
00:33:32.478 --> 00:33:35.752
So he said, "Wes, you need to go.

743
00:33:35.752 --> 00:33:36.980
Take the truck."

744
00:33:36.980 --> 00:33:39.026
I had my own truck.

745
00:33:39.026 --> 00:33:42.299
"Go over there and pick up the mail.”

746
00:33:42.299 --> 00:33:47.619
And he said, "Bring it here and tomorrow, you going to deliver it."

747
00:33:47.619 --> 00:33:49.256
They fabricated this thing!

748
00:33:49.256 --> 00:33:54.166
And boy, here I'm thirty in the waist, forty in the chest.

749
00:33:54.166 --> 00:33:54.575
Built.

750
00:33:54.575 --> 00:33:57.849
I had a head of hair like Diamond.

751
00:33:57.849 --> 00:34:04.396
I hadn't shaved . . . I had a beard, black and white, I kept it up trimmed good.

752
00:34:04.396 --> 00:34:09.307
So when I got to the front office, I walk in there.

753
00:34:09.307 --> 00:34:11.762
I said, "What is the mail?"

754
00:34:11.762 --> 00:34:16.673
So she opened the door and she hid back of the door.

755
00:34:16.673 --> 00:34:19.128
They say, "It’s in the office.

756
00:34:19.128 --> 00:34:20.765
Go get it, Wes."

757
00:34:20.765 --> 00:34:24.448
And they had about fifteen or twenty white girls.

758
00:34:24.448 --> 00:34:26.084
They wanted to see.

759
00:34:26.084 --> 00:34:27.721
The manager was there.

760
00:34:27.721 --> 00:34:28.540
Mr. Ratliff.

761
00:34:28.540 --> 00:34:30.995
They was all waiting to see.

762
00:34:30.995 --> 00:34:35.496
So when I walk in the office she opened the door.

763
00:34:35.496 --> 00:34:38.361
Good thing I had a good heart.

764
00:34:38.361 --> 00:34:40.816
I'd have caught a heart attack.

765
00:34:40.816 --> 00:34:42.862
She fell in my arms.

766
00:34:42.862 --> 00:34:44.499
She just . . . Crocodile tears.

767
00:34:44.499 --> 00:34:46.954
I tried to talk to her.

768
00:34:46.954 --> 00:34:48.182
We couldn't talk.

769
00:34:48.182 --> 00:34:49.000
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

770
00:34:49.000 --> 00:34:49.408
<v MONTGOMERY>And . . .

771
00:34:49.408 --> 00:34:51.041
<v DIGILORMO>That's a beautiful story.

772
00:34:51.041 --> 00:34:55.122
<v MONTGOMERY>We hug, and we kiss, and she said, "Let's go."

773
00:34:55.122 --> 00:34:56.347
I said, "Okay."

774
00:34:56.347 --> 00:35:00.429
So we left, and everybody in the office was crying.

775
00:35:00.429 --> 00:35:04.102
They didn’t have a dry eye in the office.

776
00:35:04.102 --> 00:35:04.510
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

777
00:35:04.510 --> 00:35:05.735
<v MONTGOMERY>Including the manager.

778
00:35:05.735 --> 00:35:07.776
He was . . . Everybody was crying.

779
00:35:07.776 --> 00:35:08.184
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

780
00:35:08.184 --> 00:35:12.673
<v MONTGOMERY>Walk out the office went in the corner and we left.

781
00:35:12.673 --> 00:35:15.939
And she stayed here for about a month.

782
00:35:15.939 --> 00:35:20.837
"I got to go back to Los Angeles, go meet your husband."

783
00:35:20.837 --> 00:35:22.878
He was in the service.

784
00:35:22.878 --> 00:35:26.143
He had a big job in the service.

785
00:35:26.143 --> 00:35:29.000
<v DIGILORMO>Were you ever in the service?

786
00:35:29.000 --> 00:35:29.333
<v MONTGOMERY>Never.

787
00:35:29.333 --> 00:35:30.333
Never did, no.

788
00:35:30.333 --> 00:35:30.667
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

789
00:35:30.667 --> 00:35:35.000
<v MONTGOMERY>No, I told them, if I went [ . . .?] keep me for twenty years.[ . . .?] Yeah.

790
00:35:35.000 --> 00:35:39.000
They brought me to New Orleans when I was eighteen years old.

791
00:35:39.000 --> 00:35:41.333
<v DIGILORMO>And that was for the Korean War?

792
00:35:41.333 --> 00:35:41.667
<v MONTGOMERY>Yeah.

793
00:35:41.667 --> 00:35:42.000
Vietnam.

794
00:35:42.000 --> 00:35:42.667
<v DIGILORMO>Oh, Vietnam.

795
00:35:42.667 --> 00:35:43.000
Okay.

796
00:35:43.000 --> 00:35:47.000
<v MONTGOMERY>Yeah, and they kept me there about a month in New Orleans.

797
00:35:47.000 --> 00:35:49.667
Wouldn't let me come back to Lake Charles.

798
00:35:49.667 --> 00:35:54.333
They said I had too much . . . I told them I didn't go to school.

799
00:35:54.333 --> 00:35:56.000
I couldn't read and write.

800
00:35:56.000 --> 00:35:57.333
I wish I didn’t.

801
00:35:57.333 --> 00:35:58.000
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

802
00:35:58.000 --> 00:36:01.048
<v MONTGOMERY>But they say, "Your IQ is too high.

803
00:36:01.048 --> 00:36:04.095
You got the highest IQ we ever had."

804
00:36:04.095 --> 00:36:06.381
I didn't know what that was.

805
00:36:06.381 --> 00:36:06.762
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

806
00:36:06.762 --> 00:36:07.905
<v MONTGOMERY>I was smart.

807
00:36:07.905 --> 00:36:08.286
<v DIGILORMO>Right.

808
00:36:08.286 --> 00:36:11.333
<v MONTOGMERY>I was the smartest man they had there.

809
00:36:11.333 --> 00:36:13.238
But I didn't know it.

810
00:36:13.238 --> 00:36:14.000
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

811
00:36:14.000 --> 00:36:18.282
<v MONTOGMERY>And when I come back I had somebody to look into the history book.

812
00:36:18.282 --> 00:36:19.506
How you call it?

813
00:36:19.506 --> 00:36:20.118
Your dictionary.

814
00:36:20.118 --> 00:36:21.953
I said, "What is the IQ?"

815
00:36:21.953 --> 00:36:24.094
They said, "Wes, that's the smart man."

816
00:36:24.094 --> 00:36:25.012
I said, "What?"

817
00:36:25.012 --> 00:36:25.929
They said, "Why?"

818
00:36:25.929 --> 00:36:32.047
I said, "Well in New Orleans they wouldn't let me leave New Orleans, they kept me there for a month.

819
00:36:32.047 --> 00:36:32.965
Maybe two months.

820
00:36:32.965 --> 00:36:34.188
Wouldn't let me leave.

821
00:36:34.188 --> 00:36:36.329
They said I was lying to them.”

822
00:36:36.329 --> 00:36:39.694
This is the highest IQ they’d ever had in New Orleans.

823
00:36:39.694 --> 00:36:43.976
<v DIGILORMO>And they thought you were lying about not being able to read or write?

824
00:36:43.976 --> 00:36:44.282
<v MONTGOMERY>Yeah.

825
00:36:44.282 --> 00:36:45.812
So they came to Duson.

826
00:36:45.812 --> 00:36:47.341
They come see my record.

827
00:36:47.341 --> 00:36:49.176
I went to school one year.

828
00:36:49.176 --> 00:36:50.094
Bob and Nancy.

829
00:36:50.094 --> 00:36:51.624
That was the little book.

830
00:36:51.624 --> 00:36:52.235
<v DIGILORMO>That book.

831
00:36:52.235 --> 00:36:53.153
<v MONTGOMERY>Bob and Nancy.

832
00:36:53.153 --> 00:36:55.600
And the pictures in the book in front.

833
00:36:55.600 --> 00:36:58.047
And I didn't go to school no more.

834
00:36:58.047 --> 00:36:58.353
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

835
00:36:58.353 --> 00:36:59.882
<v MONTGOMERY>So they came to Duson.

836
00:36:59.882 --> 00:37:06.000
And they come back in the front of the draft committee and say, "Yeah, you didn't go to school."

837
00:37:06.000 --> 00:37:08.077
<v DIGILORMO>And then they let you go?

838
00:37:08.077 --> 00:37:09.462
<v MONTGOMERY>They let me go.

839
00:37:09.462 --> 00:37:11.192
They paid for my motel.

840
00:37:11.192 --> 00:37:14.308
They paid for everything for me to stay there.

841
00:37:14.308 --> 00:37:17.423
They paid for my bus to come back here.

842
00:37:17.423 --> 00:37:18.808
They paid for everything.

843
00:37:18.808 --> 00:37:22.269
They say, "You the smartest man we ever had here."

844
00:37:22.269 --> 00:37:24.692
I was just an old country boy.

845
00:37:24.692 --> 00:37:25.038
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

846
00:37:25.038 --> 00:37:27.462
<v MONTGOMERY>Didn't know that God . . . It wasn't me.

847
00:37:27.462 --> 00:37:29.192
God had that in me.

848
00:37:29.192 --> 00:37:29.538
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

849
00:37:29.538 --> 00:37:33.000
<v MONTGOMERY>You know God had me . . . Nobody could touch me.

850
00:37:33.000 --> 00:37:35.786
<v DIGILORMO>So were you too young for the Korean War?

851
00:37:35.786 --> 00:37:36.095
<v MONTGOMERY>[Pardon]?

852
00:37:36.095 --> 00:37:39.500
<v DIGILORMO>Where you too young to be drafted for the Korean War?

853
00:37:39.500 --> 00:37:45.381
<v MONTGOMERY>Well what happened, when they were taking people to war . . . What they told me, they wanted nobody wasn't educated.

854
00:37:45.381 --> 00:37:46.000
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

855
00:37:46.000 --> 00:37:49.043
<v MONTGOMERY>But every . . . One day we went there we was thirty-two.

856
00:37:49.043 --> 00:37:52.391
It was about eight or ten that couldn't read and write.

857
00:37:52.391 --> 00:37:54.217
We all stayed here including me.

858
00:37:54.217 --> 00:37:54.522
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

859
00:37:54.522 --> 00:37:55.739
<v MONTGOMERY>They took everybody else.

860
00:37:55.739 --> 00:37:56.652
<v DIGILORMO>I got you.

861
00:37:56.652 --> 00:37:58.783
<v MONTGOMERY>So that's how I survived the war.

862
00:37:58.783 --> 00:37:59.087
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

863
00:37:59.087 --> 00:37:59.696
<v MONTGOMERY>No schooling.

864
00:37:59.696 --> 00:38:00.000
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

865
00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:05.478
<v MONTGOMERY>If I'd have been . . . Because they told me if I was lying, they put me in the frontline.

866
00:38:05.478 --> 00:38:08.522
That’s what that . . . Wes . . . I’ll take it to my graveyard.

867
00:38:08.522 --> 00:38:12.174
They say, "We find out you lying, because we going to Duson . . ."

868
00:38:12.174 --> 00:38:12.478
<v DIGILORMO>Wow.

869
00:38:12.478 --> 00:38:17.652
<v MONTOGMERY>And they say, "If we find out you lying, we going to put you in the frontline."

870
00:38:17.652 --> 00:38:21.000
That mean I'd have got killed when I got there.

871
00:38:21.000 --> 00:38:23.143
<v DIGILORMO>They really didn't believe you.

872
00:38:23.143 --> 00:38:23.571
<v MONTGOMERY>No!

873
00:38:23.571 --> 00:38:27.857
But they came down, they told me they was sorry.

874
00:38:27.857 --> 00:38:30.429
Said, "You're just a smart man."

875
00:38:30.429 --> 00:38:34.286
<v DIGILORMO>Well let's . . . We got off track a little bit.

876
00:38:34.286 --> 00:38:34.714
<v MONTGOMERY>Yeah.

877
00:38:34.714 --> 00:38:37.714
<v DIGILORMO>Let's talk about Mossville for a second.

878
00:38:37.714 --> 00:38:39.429
So your brother Valery.

879
00:38:39.429 --> 00:38:42.000
Does he still live there?

880
00:38:42.000 --> 00:38:42.387
<v MONTGOMERY>Yeah.

881
00:38:42.387 --> 00:38:43.933
He still live there.

882
00:38:43.933 --> 00:38:45.480
He's ninety years old.

883
00:38:45.480 --> 00:38:47.413
<v DIGILORMO>He, still lives in Mossville?

884
00:38:47.413 --> 00:38:50.120
<v MONTGOMERY>One of them old timers, you know.

885
00:38:50.120 --> 00:38:50.507
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

886
00:38:50.507 --> 00:38:52.053
What was his role?

887
00:38:52.053 --> 00:38:58.240
I know you said you went for work . . . You went and he got you a job.

888
00:38:58.240 --> 00:38:58.627
Correct?

889
00:38:58.627 --> 00:38:59.013
<v MONTGOMERY>Yeah.

890
00:38:59.013 --> 00:39:00.947
<v DIGILORMO>When you were a teenager.

891
00:39:00.947 --> 00:39:02.493
<v MONTGOMERY>I was a teenager.

892
00:39:02.493 --> 00:39:05.973
Conoco Refinery called for me to go to work.

893
00:39:05.973 --> 00:39:11.000
<v DIGILORMO>Okay, but that was after you were in Mossville for a while.

894
00:39:11.000 --> 00:39:12.333
<v MONTGOMERY>I was in Mossville.

895
00:39:12.333 --> 00:39:14.000
Conoco wanted to hire me.

896
00:39:14.000 --> 00:39:15.333
They didn't want Valery.

897
00:39:15.333 --> 00:39:16.667
<v DIGILORMO>They didn't want Valery.

898
00:39:16.667 --> 00:39:17.000
<v MONTGOMERY>No.

899
00:39:17.000 --> 00:39:17.667
<v DIGILORMO>How come?

900
00:39:17.667 --> 00:39:19.667
<v MONTGOMERY>Well because they . . . It was Jesus.

901
00:39:19.667 --> 00:39:20.000
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

902
00:39:20.000 --> 00:39:21.333
<v MONTGOMERY>They come after me.

903
00:39:21.333 --> 00:39:22.000
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

904
00:39:22.000 --> 00:39:24.815
<v MONTOGMERY>So I told Mr. [Lyon?] LeBlanc the supervisor.

905
00:39:24.815 --> 00:39:27.981
I said, "Why don't you all hire my brother?

906
00:39:27.981 --> 00:39:29.389
He got five children."

907
00:39:29.389 --> 00:39:31.500
I said, "I'm a single man."

908
00:39:31.500 --> 00:39:31.852
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

909
00:39:31.852 --> 00:39:33.259
<v MONTGOMERY>"Come get me later."

910
00:39:33.259 --> 00:39:35.722
"Wes," he said, "They don't want Valery."

911
00:39:35.722 --> 00:39:40.648
So after we kept . . . I kept talking to him for a couple of weeks.

912
00:39:40.648 --> 00:39:42.407
They said, "We'll hire him."

913
00:39:42.407 --> 00:39:44.870
So they hired Valery in my place.

914
00:39:44.870 --> 00:39:45.222
<v DIGILORMO>Wow.

915
00:39:45.222 --> 00:39:48.037
<v MONTGOMERY>So Valery was there about five, six years.

916
00:39:48.037 --> 00:39:51.907
They come back to Valery and say, "We still want Wes."

917
00:39:51.907 --> 00:39:57.889
Well they hadn't hired a black man in ten years, you got to understand what I'm saying.

918
00:39:57.889 --> 00:40:00.000
<v DIGILORMO>What year was that about?

919
00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:03.600
<v MONTGOMERY>Had to be . . . Let's see . . . I married in 1956.

920
00:40:03.600 --> 00:40:04.400
At twenty-two.

921
00:40:04.400 --> 00:40:07.200
So you have to back that up.

922
00:40:07.200 --> 00:40:09.600
That had to be around forty-nine.

923
00:40:09.600 --> 00:40:10.400
I guess.

924
00:40:10.400 --> 00:40:10.800
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

925
00:40:10.800 --> 00:40:13.600
<v MONTGOMERY>Because you had to back it up.

926
00:40:13.600 --> 00:40:14.000
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

927
00:40:14.000 --> 00:40:14.800
<v MONTGOMERY>You see.

928
00:40:14.800 --> 00:40:17.600
So my brother come to get me.

929
00:40:17.600 --> 00:40:21.600
He said, "Conoco still wants you to come to work."

930
00:40:21.600 --> 00:40:23.600
So I went to work.

931
00:40:23.600 --> 00:40:28.400
And once I got there the plant fell in love with me.

932
00:40:28.400 --> 00:40:32.400
They had never hired a black man in ten years.

933
00:40:32.400 --> 00:40:33.200
Just white.

934
00:40:33.200 --> 00:40:33.600
<v DIGILORMO>Right.

935
00:40:33.600 --> 00:40:34.400
<v MONTGOMERY>Terminate them.

936
00:40:34.400 --> 00:40:38.000
They'd hire blacks, but every year they'd terminate you.

937
00:40:38.000 --> 00:40:40.800
And they'd rehire you . . . like my brother.

938
00:40:40.800 --> 00:40:43.200
He had been there five years.

939
00:40:43.200 --> 00:40:45.200
Every year they'd terminate him.

940
00:40:45.200 --> 00:40:46.400
Rehire him again.

941
00:40:46.400 --> 00:40:48.000
You couldn't do nothing.

942
00:40:48.000 --> 00:40:49.200
That's the law.

943
00:40:49.200 --> 00:40:50.000
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

944
00:40:50.000 --> 00:40:54.041
<v MONTGOMERY>But when I got there, God said, "No, not this guy.

945
00:40:54.041 --> 00:40:54.408
Him.

946
00:40:54.408 --> 00:40:55.143
Not him."

947
00:40:55.143 --> 00:40:56.245
That was Jesus.

948
00:40:56.245 --> 00:40:58.082
And my boss told me.

949
00:40:58.082 --> 00:41:01.755
Said, "Wes, they want you to go in the plant."

950
00:41:01.755 --> 00:41:02.122
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

951
00:41:02.122 --> 00:41:03.592
<v MONTGOMERY>I said, "What for?"

952
00:41:03.592 --> 00:41:06.898
He said, "Well, they want you in the plant."

953
00:41:06.898 --> 00:41:08.000
They watching you.

954
00:41:08.000 --> 00:41:10.571
They never seen a man like you.”

955
00:41:10.571 --> 00:41:11.673
I said, "What?"

956
00:41:11.673 --> 00:41:14.245
He said, "Yeah, they got them binoculars.

957
00:41:14.245 --> 00:41:16.082
They watching everywhere you go."

958
00:41:16.082 --> 00:41:17.184
I said, "Okay."

959
00:41:17.184 --> 00:41:19.388
So I went in the plant.

960
00:41:19.388 --> 00:41:23.429
Within six month he said, "They want to put you permanent."

961
00:41:23.429 --> 00:41:27.102
It was ten years they hadn’t hired a black man.

962
00:41:27.102 --> 00:41:28.571
It was my uncle.

963
00:41:28.571 --> 00:41:29.673
My mom's brother.

964
00:41:29.673 --> 00:41:30.408
Ten years.

965
00:41:30.408 --> 00:41:30.776
<v DIGILORMO>Wow.

966
00:41:30.776 --> 00:41:32.245
<v MONTGOMERY>And I say, "Okay."

967
00:41:32.245 --> 00:41:38.122
<v DIGILORMO>So I'm sorry to interrupt, but if your mother's uncle worked at . . . He worked at Conoco?

968
00:41:38.122 --> 00:41:38.490
<v MONTGOMERY>Yeah.

969
00:41:38.490 --> 00:41:39.224
Edward [Babineaux?].

970
00:41:39.224 --> 00:41:41.796
<v DIGILORMO>Did he live in Mossville as well?

971
00:41:41.796 --> 00:41:44.000
