So they had a black guy, he had done got in there, Joe [Hayes?].

1446
01:02:23.080 --> 01:02:27.425
So Joe Hayes seen that our boss wanted to help me.

1447
01:02:27.425 --> 01:02:29.795
So he got up the office.

1448
01:02:29.795 --> 01:02:32.560
He said, "Wes, go lock the door.

1449
01:02:32.560 --> 01:02:33.745
Go lock it."

1450
01:02:33.745 --> 01:02:36.510
So I went and locked the door.

1451
01:02:36.510 --> 01:02:39.275
So it was just me and him.

1452
01:02:39.275 --> 01:02:40.460
"Wes," he said.

1453
01:02:40.460 --> 01:02:43.620
"I got three words for you to pass."

1454
01:02:43.620 --> 01:02:45.595
I said, "What is it?"

1455
01:02:45.595 --> 01:02:48.360
He said, "Rice, ice, and a rat."

1456
01:02:48.360 --> 01:02:51.915
I couldn't do either one of them damn things.

1457
01:02:51.915 --> 01:02:55.865
"Wes,” he said, “That nothing but a three letter word.

1458
01:02:55.865 --> 01:02:56.260
Wes."

1459
01:02:56.260 --> 01:02:57.840
He said, "Come on."

1460
01:02:57.840 --> 01:03:00.210
The man wanted me, you know.

1461
01:03:00.210 --> 01:03:01.000
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1462
01:03:01.000 --> 01:03:02.218
<v MONTGOMERY>"Wes," he said.

1463
01:03:02.218 --> 01:03:03.436
"Come on, Wes."

1464
01:03:03.436 --> 01:03:05.872
He said, "Ice" I said, "Ice."

1465
01:03:05.872 --> 01:03:07.090
"Wes," he say.

1466
01:03:07.090 --> 01:03:08.308
"Come on, Wes."

1467
01:03:08.308 --> 01:03:09.526
He say, "I-C-E."

1468
01:03:09.526 --> 01:03:10.744
I said, "I-C-E."

1469
01:03:10.744 --> 01:03:12.368
"Wes, you got that.

1470
01:03:12.368 --> 01:03:13.180
You got

1471
01:03:13.180 --> 01:03:13.586
<c.p>that."

1472
01:03:13.586 --> 01:03:16.429
So he put a check mark down.

1473
01:03:16.429 --> 01:03:18.459
<v DIGILORMO>He gave it to you?

1474
01:03:18.459 --> 01:03:18.865
<v MONTGOMERY>Yeah!

1475
01:03:18.865 --> 01:03:20.083
<v DIGILORMO>He just . . . [Laughs]

1476
01:03:20.083 --> 01:03:21.301
<v MONTGOMERY>He warned me.

1477
01:03:21.301 --> 01:03:24.955
That's why he told me to lock the door.

1478
01:03:24.955 --> 01:03:25.361
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1479
01:03:25.361 --> 01:03:26.579
<v MONTGOMERY>He said, "Rat."

1480
01:03:26.579 --> 01:03:27.391
God damn.

1481
01:03:27.391 --> 01:03:30.233
Going in the cold in the wintertime.

1482
01:03:30.233 --> 01:03:33.075
I’m sweating drops big as a crocodile.

1483
01:03:33.075 --> 01:03:37.135
“Wes,” he said, "R." I said, "R." He said, "R-A-T."

1484
01:03:37.135 --> 01:03:38.759
I said, "R- A-T."

1485
01:03:38.759 --> 01:03:39.977
He said, “Rat.

1486
01:03:39.977 --> 01:03:41.602
See, you got it.

1487
01:03:41.602 --> 01:03:42.820
You got two.

1488
01:03:42.820 --> 01:03:45.256
You got one more to go."

1489
01:03:45.256 --> 01:03:46.474
He said, "Rice.

1490
01:03:46.474 --> 01:03:46.880
Rice.

1491
01:03:46.880 --> 01:03:50.940
Oh, Wes, you got two you got one to go."

1492
01:03:50.940 --> 01:03:57.030
I was sitting there, goddamn, it was so cold and I'm sweating drops like that.

1493
01:03:57.030 --> 01:03:58.248
"Wes," he said.

1494
01:03:58.248 --> 01:04:00.278
"I know you can . . . Rice."

1495
01:04:00.278 --> 01:04:01.496
"Wes," he said.

1496
01:04:01.496 --> 01:04:04.338
"R." I said, "R." He said, "R-I.”

1497
01:04:04.338 --> 01:04:05.556
I said, “R-I.”

1498
01:04:05.556 --> 01:04:05.962
“R-I-C-E."

1499
01:04:05.962 --> 01:04:07.180
I said, "R-I-C-E."

1500
01:04:07.180 --> 01:04:12.053
He says, "You got all three of them you made a hundred."

1501
01:04:12.053 --> 01:04:13.677
He written a hundred.

1502
01:04:13.677 --> 01:04:19.767
He said, "Bring it to Mr. Clyde [Stode?] and [Matt Clemens?] at the front office."

1503
01:04:19.767 --> 01:04:22.203
He said, "You made a hundred.

1504
01:04:22.203 --> 01:04:23.827
Bring it to them."

1505
01:04:23.827 --> 01:04:29.105
So boy, I go out there with Mr. Matt Clemens and Mr. Clyde.

1506
01:04:29.105 --> 01:04:35.602
And they knew damn well . . . They knew when I signed up I didn't go to school.

1507
01:04:35.602 --> 01:04:38.038
Oh they say, "Wes you ain't [ . . .?]."

1508
01:04:38.038 --> 01:04:42.910
They said, "Oh, Wes Montgomery, told us you couldn't read and write.

1509
01:04:42.910 --> 01:04:44.940
Look, you made a hundred."

1510
01:04:44.940 --> 01:04:46.158
I couldn't say

1511
01:04:46.158 --> 01:04:46.564
<c.p>shit.

1512
01:04:46.564 --> 01:04:49.000
I couldn't say a word.

1513
01:04:49.000 --> 01:04:51.308
<v DIGILORMO>They were poking fun at you.

1514
01:04:51.308 --> 01:04:54.000
<v MONTGOMERY>Yeah, they were poking fun at me!

1515
01:04:54.000 --> 01:04:57.846
They said, "Wes, we going to put you in transportation."

1516
01:04:57.846 --> 01:05:02.846
I said . . . He said, "As of Monday you going to Mr. Joe [Conahan?]."

1517
01:05:02.846 --> 01:05:07.462
But now this is what the black did for me. [Dallas Frank?].

1518
01:05:07.462 --> 01:05:10.538
All these guys that couldn’t read and write.

1519
01:05:10.538 --> 01:05:13.231
So John F. Kennedy and Bobby Kennedy.

1520
01:05:13.231 --> 01:05:15.923
What they did . . . They got a tutor.

1521
01:05:15.923 --> 01:05:17.846
A teacher from Baton Rouge.

1522
01:05:17.846 --> 01:05:25.154
Three time a week to come to Conoco and teach all these dummy black that couldn't read and write.

1523
01:05:25.154 --> 01:05:29.769
Come teach them how to read and write. [. . . ?] know about the Kennedys.

1524
01:05:29.769 --> 01:05:32.462
But now both of you all know.

1525
01:05:32.462 --> 01:05:33.615
They got tutors.

1526
01:05:33.615 --> 01:05:35.154
Not from Lake Charles.

1527
01:05:35.154 --> 01:05:36.308
From Baton Rouge!

1528
01:05:36.308 --> 01:05:42.077
Drove here three times a week to tutor all us black . . . I call them dummies.

1529
01:05:42.077 --> 01:05:44.000
Couldn't read or write.

1530
01:05:44.000 --> 01:05:45.774
<v DIGILORMO>Well you say dummy.

1531
01:05:45.774 --> 01:05:48.435
I understand what you mean but . . .

1532
01:05:48.435 --> 01:05:50.653
<v MONTGOMERY>Yeah, didn't go to school.

1533
01:05:50.653 --> 01:05:51.097
<v DIGILORMO>Illiterate.

1534
01:05:51.097 --> 01:05:51.540
Yeah.

1535
01:05:51.540 --> 01:05:55.976
<v MONTGOMERY>So let me tell you what the black did me.

1536
01:05:55.976 --> 01:05:58.194
Now this wasn't white folks.

1537
01:05:58.194 --> 01:06:05.734
It was black. [Dallas Frank?] and Frank [Petrie?] and Wilson [ . . .?] none of them couldn’t read or write.

1538
01:06:05.734 --> 01:06:11.056
Conoco hired . . . Had hired a whole black . . . nobody could read and write.

1539
01:06:11.056 --> 01:06:14.605
They wouldn’t hire nobody that went to school.

1540
01:06:14.605 --> 01:06:15.935
I was included.

1541
01:06:15.935 --> 01:06:19.484
So we got there and they say, "Well

1542
01:06:19.484 --> 01:06:26.137
<c.p>we going to have to put you all in school for three times a week.”

1543
01:06:26.137 --> 01:06:31.460
So Dallas Frank, don't you know, they went to the front office.

1544
01:06:31.460 --> 01:06:35.452
Got the union to file some agreement against me.

1545
01:06:35.452 --> 01:06:38.113
Sure, and I'm black like them!

1546
01:06:38.113 --> 01:06:39.000
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1547
01:06:39.000 --> 01:06:42.341
<v MONTGOMERY>But they knew I couldn't read and write.

1548
01:06:42.341 --> 01:06:42.759
<v DIGILORMO>Jealous . . .

1549
01:06:42.759 --> 01:06:45.682
<v MONTGOMERY>Why could I move and they can’t?

1550
01:06:45.682 --> 01:06:46.100
<v DIGILORMO>Right.

1551
01:06:46.100 --> 01:06:50.276
<v MONTGOMERY>But God had me . . . Jesus had me in his hand.

1552
01:06:50.276 --> 01:06:52.782
You can't do nothing with God.

1553
01:06:52.782 --> 01:07:03.641
You know what Mr. Hank [Clemens?] and Clyde Stewart the personnel manager . . . They went to the Mossville High School and talked to the principal Mr. [Almstar?].

1554
01:07:03.641 --> 01:07:07.400
They said, "Look, would you mind working with us?

1555
01:07:07.400 --> 01:07:11.159
Wes Montgomery is uneducated; he didn't go to school.

1556
01:07:11.159 --> 01:07:16.171
But we putting him up to get a big job in transportation.

1557
01:07:16.171 --> 01:07:17.841
He's a smart man.

1558
01:07:17.841 --> 01:07:19.512
He can do anything.

1559
01:07:19.512 --> 01:07:22.435
He can handle all them heavy equipment."

1560
01:07:22.435 --> 01:07:27.447
He said, "This man can do anything, but I need your help."

1561
01:07:27.447 --> 01:07:32.876
He say, "Can we fix some papers like he went to school here?"

1562
01:07:32.876 --> 01:07:34.547
"Oh, yeah," he said.

1563
01:07:34.547 --> 01:07:36.635
"That ain't nothing to do."

1564
01:07:36.635 --> 01:07:44.571
Shit, he got that book and type them out some letter and nothing they could do about that shit.

1565
01:07:44.571 --> 01:07:47.494
None of them could read and write.

1566
01:07:47.494 --> 01:07:50.000
Shit, you figured them papers . . .

1567
01:07:50.000 --> 01:07:54.836
<v DIGILORMO>So you didn't have to go to those classes because of that?

1568
01:07:54.836 --> 01:07:55.239
<v MONTGOMERY>No!

1569
01:07:55.239 --> 01:07:58.866
Shit, them white folks fix it up for me!

1570
01:07:58.866 --> 01:08:05.716
I'm telling you them white people, get with the right one they can get anything you want!

1571
01:08:05.716 --> 01:08:07.328
And they got it.

1572
01:08:07.328 --> 01:08:08.940
I got in transportation.

1573
01:08:08.940 --> 01:08:09.343
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1574
01:08:09.343 --> 01:08:12.970
<v MONTGOMERY>I had a raise . . . Forty dollars a week raise.

1575
01:08:12.970 --> 01:08:16.194
Overtime . . . A hundred dollars a week with overtime.

1576
01:08:16.194 --> 01:08:17.000
<v DIGILORMO>Wow.

1577
01:08:17.000 --> 01:08:17.878
<v MONTGOMERY>That's right.

1578
01:08:17.878 --> 01:08:20.514
I stayed there until I retired.

1579
01:08:20.514 --> 01:08:20.953
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1580
01:08:20.953 --> 01:08:25.345
<v MONTGOMERY>Until I retired when I made forty-four. [. . . ?] Going into business.

1581
01:08:25.345 --> 01:08:25.784
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1582
01:08:25.784 --> 01:08:26.662
<v MONTGOMERY>That's right.

1583
01:08:26.662 --> 01:08:27.101
<v DIGILORMO>Wow.

1584
01:08:27.101 --> 01:08:29.297
<v MONTGOMERY>That’s what I’m telling you.

1585
01:08:29.297 --> 01:08:34.568
When God is with you, you can always . . . You can make it.

1586
01:08:34.568 --> 01:08:35.007
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1587
01:08:35.007 --> 01:08:37.203
<v MONTGOMERY>And who got me there?

1588
01:08:37.203 --> 01:08:38.081
White people.

1589
01:08:38.081 --> 01:08:38.959
Not black.

1590
01:08:38.959 --> 01:08:41.155
Black was holding me down.

1591
01:08:41.155 --> 01:08:43.351
White folks brought me up.

1592
01:08:43.351 --> 01:08:45.108
They passed my physical.

1593
01:08:45.108 --> 01:08:48.622
I couldn’t pass my physical . . . Passed my physical.

1594
01:08:48.622 --> 01:08:49.939
They signed everything.

1595
01:08:49.939 --> 01:08:51.696
I got in transportation.

1596
01:08:51.696 --> 01:08:53.453
It's all white again.

1597
01:08:53.453 --> 01:08:54.331
All white.

1598
01:08:54.331 --> 01:08:56.088
They gave me everything.

1599
01:08:56.088 --> 01:09:02.676
I mean . . . And here I'm dating the finest white woman they got on the job.

1600
01:09:02.676 --> 01:09:05.750
Ain't nothing . . . They had a white woman [ . . .?].

1601
01:09:05.750 --> 01:09:07.507
That was a machine.

1602
01:09:07.507 --> 01:09:11.459
Any man would give his right arm for that.

1603
01:09:11.459 --> 01:09:14.973
So it was white folks all the way.

1604
01:09:14.973 --> 01:09:21.122
It was just the way that people took care of me my whole life.

1605
01:09:21.122 --> 01:09:22.000
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1606
01:09:22.000 --> 01:09:22.445
<v MONTGOMERY>Yeah.

1607
01:09:22.445 --> 01:09:26.454
And let me tell you what happened to Mossville.

1608
01:09:26.454 --> 01:09:28.681
You need to know that.

1609
01:09:28.681 --> 01:09:31.798
We didn't have no water in Mossville.

1610
01:09:31.798 --> 01:09:32.244
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

1611
01:09:32.244 --> 01:09:34.471
When you first moved there?

1612
01:09:34.471 --> 01:09:35.361
<v MONTGOMERY>No water.

1613
01:09:35.361 --> 01:09:35.807
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

1614
01:09:35.807 --> 01:09:39.370
<v MONTGOMERY>So we lost between four and six kids.

1615
01:09:39.370 --> 01:09:42.933
Well the health department in Lake Charles say,

1616
01:09:42.933 --> 01:09:50.059
"The reason why them children is dying . . . Nobody had no money to dig no deep well."

1617
01:09:50.059 --> 01:09:53.622
The little old well was twenty-four foot down.

1618
01:09:53.622 --> 01:10:00.748
When a snake died or frog died, well that shit all go back in the well.

1619
01:10:00.748 --> 01:10:04.311
The health department checked them children had died.

1620
01:10:04.311 --> 01:10:06.983
He said, "That's from the water.

1621
01:10:06.983 --> 01:10:07.429
Contaminated."

1622
01:10:07.429 --> 01:10:10.101
President Johnson . . . He was the president.

1623
01:10:10.101 --> 01:10:11.437
Lyndon Baines Johnson.

1624
01:10:11.437 --> 01:10:15.000
<v DIGILORMO>So this is back in the sixties?

1625
01:10:15.000 --> 01:10:15.438
<v MONTGOMERY>Yeah.

1626
01:10:15.438 --> 01:10:18.062
Governor [Edwin] Edwards was the governor.

1627
01:10:18.062 --> 01:10:23.750
One of the best governors they ever had in the state of Louisiana.

1628
01:10:23.750 --> 01:10:27.250
He's the best . . . And he was my brother.

1629
01:10:27.250 --> 01:10:27.688
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1630
01:10:27.688 --> 01:10:29.875
<v MONTGOMERY>The man is . . . I'm eighty-one.

1631
01:10:29.875 --> 01:10:31.188
He's about ninety-two.

1632
01:10:31.188 --> 01:10:33.812
And married a little white girl.

1633
01:10:33.812 --> 01:10:38.188
She thirty-six years old and got a baby for him.

1634
01:10:38.188 --> 01:10:39.500
And a boy!

1635
01:10:39.500 --> 01:10:39.938
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1636
01:10:39.938 --> 01:10:41.250
<v MONTGOMERY>You believe that?

1637
01:10:41.250 --> 01:10:42.125
A boy!

1638
01:10:42.125 --> 01:10:45.188
You see, a man's sperm never dies.

1639
01:10:45.188 --> 01:10:48.688
See a man's sperm . . . People don't know that.

1640
01:10:48.688 --> 01:10:50.438
His sperm lives forever.

1641
01:10:50.438 --> 01:10:53.500
But a woman when she reach forty-

1642
01:10:53.500 --> 01:10:57.438
<c.p>five she can throw her deck in the card.

1643
01:10:57.438 --> 01:10:58.312
She's through.

1644
01:10:58.312 --> 01:11:02.688
Maybe once in a blue moon she may get pregnant.

1645
01:11:02.688 --> 01:11:07.500
But if she hasn't been pregnant before, that's all over with.

1646
01:11:07.500 --> 01:11:07.938
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1647
01:11:07.938 --> 01:11:11.000
So children were dying in Mossville?

1648
01:11:11.000 --> 01:11:11.839
<v MONTGOMERY>Oh, yes!

1649
01:11:11.839 --> 01:11:13.097
<v DIGILORMO>In the sixties?

1650
01:11:13.097 --> 01:11:13.516
<v MONTGOMERY>Dying!

1651
01:11:13.516 --> 01:11:13.935
Yes.

1652
01:11:13.935 --> 01:11:14.355
Died.

1653
01:11:14.355 --> 01:11:19.387
<v DIGILORMO>And they were saying it was because the wells were too shallow?

1654
01:11:19.387 --> 01:11:19.806
<v MONTGOMERY>Contaminated.

1655
01:11:19.806 --> 01:11:20.645
<v DIGILORMO>Was contaminated.

1656
01:11:20.645 --> 01:11:24.000
But not with chemicals, with organic material?

1657
01:11:24.000 --> 01:11:27.836
<v MONTGOMERY>No, no. There was some snakes, frogs that died.

1658
01:11:27.836 --> 01:11:31.672
And once they died leaked back in the well.

1659
01:11:31.672 --> 01:11:42.328
It could have been from chemical and whatnot but they said it’s from animal that die in the ground in the . . . Well it makes sense.

1660
01:11:42.328 --> 01:11:47.016
Take a leak back in the well, you’re drinking that crap.

1661
01:11:47.016 --> 01:11:47.443
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1662
01:11:47.443 --> 01:11:52.131
<v MONTGOMERY>But now me and my brother we were working at Conoco.

1663
01:11:52.131 --> 01:11:55.115
Well we had some wells five-hundred foot.

1664
01:11:55.115 --> 01:11:56.820
We had big job.

1665
01:11:56.820 --> 01:11:58.525
We could afford wells.

1666
01:11:58.525 --> 01:12:05.770
So we give . . . We’d furnish water to some of our neighbor, because we had a deep well.

1667
01:12:05.770 --> 01:12:08.328
My well was over five-hundred foot.

1668
01:12:08.328 --> 01:12:09.180
Oh, shit.

1669
01:12:09.180 --> 01:12:12.164
I could furnish water to the city.

1670
01:12:12.164 --> 01:12:12.590
So . . .

1671
01:12:12.590 --> 01:12:16.000
<v DIGILORMO>How many people would you share with?

1672
01:12:16.000 --> 01:12:19.171
<v MONTGOMERY>Four . . . [. . . ?]Three or four people with me in my well.

1673
01:12:19.171 --> 01:12:21.390
And my brother did the same thing.

1674
01:12:21.390 --> 01:12:21.707
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1675
01:12:21.707 --> 01:12:22.024
Okay.

1676
01:12:22.024 --> 01:12:23.610
<v MONTGOMERY>We both had deep wells.

1677
01:12:23.610 --> 01:12:23.927
<v DIGILORMO>Good.

1678
01:12:23.927 --> 01:12:25.512
<v MONTGOMERY>We both worked for Conoco.

1679
01:12:25.512 --> 01:12:29.000
<v DIGILORMO>You all lived next to each other at this point?

1680
01:12:29.000 --> 01:12:29.735
<v MONTGOMERY>Not far.

1681
01:12:29.735 --> 01:12:34.510
We was about . . . Me and my brother was I'd say about a block.

1682
01:12:34.510 --> 01:12:35.612
A city block.

1683
